  "rationale": "The only full-album meeting between Milt Jackson and John Coltrane, captured in one January 1959 session. Coltrane was between Prestige and his early Atlantic solo dates; Jackson was at his most lyrical outside the MJQ. The rhythm section of Hank Jones, Paul Chambers, and Connie Kay creates a relaxed, swinging foundation that lets both soloists stretch. Consensus canonical \u2014 Penguin Guide core, a staple in 'essential jazz collaborations' lists. Released 1961 on Atlantic SD-1368.",
